# plan

**Project overlay:** if `docs/process/commands/plan.local.md` exists, read it
before you start — the project's own rules for this command, binding over
this file where it says so; a template doc this command sends you to may
have one beside it (`<doc>.local.md`), read with the doc
(`docs/process/overlays.md`).

Turn an approved design into a testable task breakdown. Read
`docs/process/workflow.md` (Plan) and `docs/process/journal-state-plans.md`.
{% if modules.speckit %}Run `/speckit-plan` + `/speckit-tasks`; add `tier: N` and `issue: <ref>`
lines to `specs/<feature>/plan.md`; `/speckit-analyze` is optional, on demand, like `-checklist`
(`docs/process/modules/speckit.md`).
{% else %}The design must be clarification-free: no unresolved `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]`
marker survives into a plan (the `clarification` gate blocks it).
{% endif %}Required for Tier 2+. The plan names the decisions each touched section of
`docs/process/review-checklist.md` asks for (its **Plan decides:** lines) and checks every
signature it cites against the code. Commit the plan and run the gates
(`uv run scripts/process/gate_runner.py`) before you build its review bundle — the bundle runs
no preflight, and a red gate found after the review costs a second round. Before `planned`, a
Tier 2+ plan is reviewed once,
independently (`workflow.md`, Plan): Tier 2 by a fresh subagent on its bundle, attested with
`attest.py --plan-review`; Tier 3 by a dispatched plan-review session. The plan carries
`plan-session model: <your concrete model id>`; the reviewer is of no lower class and
`--model` names its concrete id (`attest.py` refuses otherwise — `verification-independence.md`,
"Evidence at the writer").
